## 5. Stability check across maturity bands

To ensure the yield is **constant** rather than maturity-dependent (which would invalidate the model), a stratification test calibrates the optimal yield separately on each residual maturity band. Results show convergence on long maturities:

| Band R | n | Local optimal yield | RMSE (days) |
|---|---|---|---|
| [1, 3[ | 45,811 | 8.22% | 29.85 |
| [3, 5[ | 39,407 | 6.21% | 31.77 |
| [5, 10[ | 36,989 | 5.46% | 38.44 |
| [10, 15[ | 18,963 | **4.99%** | 23.81 |
| [15, 20[ | 11,163 | **4.93%** | 11.29 |
| [20, 30[ | 6,329 | **4.92%** | 9.22 |

The deviation on short maturities (apparent yield inflated up to 8% on [1, 3[) does **not** reflect parameter variation but a **model absorption effect**: on this band, the ~3% cluster of atypical facilities (long deferral, hidden bullet) drags the average. Once isolated, the yield falls back to 4.95% across the board, with residual RMSE down to 9-12 days on [15, 30[ — essentially calendar noise.

