## Summary of evidence

The choice of YIELD_PIVOT_SRS = 4.95% is supported by **three independent estimates** that all converge to the same value:

| Estimation method | Result |
|---|---|
| Global RMSE minimization (n = 158,668) | 4.9546% |
| Control calibration on clean sample (n = 28) | 4.9444% |
| Per-line implied yield (median) | 5.0029% |

Combined with the rejection of the contractual-rate hypothesis through three independent angles (global RMSE 1.97x worse, stratified RMSE up to 5.80x worse on long maturities, implied yield correlation with T_INTRT ≈ 0), this provides robust empirical justification for the parameter.

